.TH UDHCPC 1 "2026" "KERNEL32" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
udhcpc \- client DHCP / DHCP client
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B udhcpc
[-i interface] [-q] [-t tries] [-T seconds]
.br
.B dhclient

.br
.SH DESCRIPTION
Minimal DHCP client over broadcast UDP: DISCOVER, OFFER, REQUEST, ACK, then configures the interface (ifconfig), the default route (route) and /etc/resolv.conf.
A single negotiation is made: leases are not renewed.
.SH SEE ALSO
ip(1), ifconfig(1)
